-- Personal data / GDPR: a STRONG rule. The e-mail is masked for EVERYONE...
-- ...EXCEPT the customer_support role, which has a legitimate business need.
--
-- How to carve an exception into a strong rule: Global Security Policies combine with
-- AND, so a second policy can NEVER unmask what a first one masked. The exception goes
-- INTO THE AUDIENCE of the rule: NOT_IN ROLES (customer_support) means the rule applies
-- to everyone whose roles are not customer_support; customer support never triggers it.
--
-- Unconditional masking: FILTER '1 = 0' (no row in clear). The class_pii tag sits on
-- the GOLD column chinook_sales.iv_invoices.email, so the e-mail is masked wherever it
-- appears downstream.
CONNECT DATABASE admin;

CREATE OR REPLACE GLOBAL_SECURITY_POLICY p_mask_email_pii
  DESCRIPTION = 'E-mail (personal data) masked for everyone except customer support'
  ENABLED = TRUE
  AUDIENCE    ( NOT_IN ROLES ( customer_support ) )
  ELEMENTS    ( COLUMNS TAGGED ANY ( class_pii ) )
  RESTRICTION ( FILTER = '1 = 0' MASKING ANY ( class_pii ) WITH ( DEFAULT ) );
